hi there everybody it's Kevin Van horde  standing in for reviewer lathe Johnson  to tell you about hearthstone the name  hearthstone refers to the white and  turquoise rock that sends World of  Warcraft players back to ends but it  also suggests friendly competition far  removed from the battles and weighty  stratagems of other one-on-one  collectible card games  if world of warcraft was the every man's  online RPG then this is the every man's  collectible card game few other card  games rival heart stones charming  personality it reveals itself in the  little things such as the way you can  fiddle with watermills on the board  while you're waiting a challengers next  move you see it in the way war crafts  most exaggerated figures guide you  through a tutorial that's as helpful as  it is fun  harsh stones great strength however is  that it welcomes you with open arms even  if you've never played the genre before  what's more it avoids caustic speech by  limiting players to preset responses  hearthstone shatters barriers to entry  while supplying the means to access  greater challenges if you seek them  harsh stone adopts the familiar model of  whittling down the opposing players hit  points with attack points from cards but  it simplifies the cumbersome resource  mechanics of other games for a mana bar  that automatically expands with the  passing of each turn it's a system  geared towards speed and hero abilities  that don't depend on carts like the  mages fireball act as wild cards that  can keep players in the fight it's a  lunch breakers game and indeed the  toughest matches rarely lasts more than  15 minutes  Blizzard blesses hearthstone with  significant depth in spite of such nods  to speed there's a wide assortment of  cards with specific abilities in play  some come from the nine unlockable decks  modeled on familiar world of warcraft  classes while others come from a massive  bundle of cards that players can use  with all the decks  a player using the hunter deck might  spring a trap by unleashing three week  snake cards after an enemy attacks four  minions her opponent might then fend off  their attacks by tossing down a tanky  card with taunt thereby forcing the  snakes to attack it instead of the main  hero still further strategies await a  mage could incapacitate the taunting  card with a frost Nova thereby letting  the player blast the hero with impunity  over time perhaps inevitably the process  of leveling and building killer decks  devolves into a grind Blizzard gives you  the option to craft your own cards to  counter the grind although it's here  where the veterans enjoy a significant  advantage over rookies hearthstone  simplifies many of the necessary actions  such as destroying excess cards and  neatly arranging the available cards in  a flipbook of sort but the uninitiated  get few clues as to what to focus on and  in the worst cases a player might waste  his material on a worthless card or  accidentally disintegrate one of the  best in his deck arena mode helps quash  the tedium arenas come with an entry fee  although it's usually negligible if you  manage to complete daily quests which  have you meeting specific goals to earn  rewards the allure of arena lies in  leveling of the playing field rather  than bringing your own decks into the  battle you're only allowed to choose  from one of three classes and then you  need to build your deck by choosing one  of the random cards hearthstone throws  at you until you complete a full deck of  30 cards the outcome can still be  outrageously imbalanced some shmuck  might seem to swim in legendary cards  while the one you have never gets drawn  from the deck of course it works both  ways  the next arena match could shower you  with Legendary's like Ragnaros instead  it's too bad there's no spectator mode  or a replay option so that you can learn  from your mistake  and the daily quests take long enough to  complete that you'll sometimes want to  fork out some cash if you want to play  in the arena but such objections are  minor in hearthstone  a game so brainy and breezy the quick  matches and marathon sessions alike are  immensely rewarding  you  [Music]
 

